.TH UENTRY 1 "2026-02-26" "uentry 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uentry \- universal container entrypoint with PID 1 supervision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uentry
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB--\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
uentry is a universal container entrypoint that handles PID 1 responsibilities:
signal forwarding, zombie process reaping, and graceful shutdown.

When containers run as PID 1, they inherit kernel responsibilities that most
applications don't handle correctly. uentry wraps your application and manages
these duties, plus provides optional security enforcement, secrets management,
and lifecycle hooks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file. Default: \fI/etc/uentry/config.yaml\fR
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile =\fINAME\fR
Built-in profile to use. Available profiles: \fIbaseline\fR, \fIk8s\fR, \fIweb\fR, \fIworker\fR
.TP
.BR \-\-strict
Enable strict fail-closed security mode. Refuses to start if:
.RS
.IP \[bu] 2
Running as root without privilege drop configuration
.IP \[bu]
Root filesystem is writable (unless \fBwritable_paths\fR configured)
.IP \[bu]
Dangerous mounts detected (docker.sock, etc.)
.IP \[bu]
Dangerous environment variables present (LD_PRELOAD, etc.)
.RE
.TP
.BR \-\-diagnose
Run system diagnostics and exit. Useful for debugging container configurations.
.TP
.BR \-\-audit
Enable audit reporting.
.TP
.BR \-\-audit\-deep
Enable deep audit tracing. Uses capability-aware fallback behavior.
.TP
.BR \-\-audit\-output =\fIPATH\fR
Write audit JSON report to the specified path.
.TP
.BR \-\-audit\-profile\-output =\fIPATH\fR
Write discovered profile snippet YAML to the specified path.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Separator between uentry options and the command to execute.
.SH PROFILES
Built-in profiles provide sensible defaults for common use cases:
.TP
.B baseline
Safe defaults for any container. Enables signal forwarding.
.TP
.B k8s
Kubernetes workloads. Allows KUBERNETES_* environment variables,
loads service account tokens, extended shutdown timeout.
.TP
.B web
HTTP servers and APIs. Configures HTTP readiness probe on /health:8080,
startup grace period, extended shutdown timeout.
.TP
.B worker
Background job processors. Extended startup and shutdown timeouts for
graceful work completion.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is loaded with the following precedence (highest to lowest):
.IP 1. 4
CLI flags
.IP 2. 4
Environment variables (\fBUENTRY_*\fR)
.IP 3. 4
Config file (\fI/etc/uentry/config.yaml\fR)
.IP 4. 4
Profile defaults
.IP 5. 4
Built-in defaults
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The configuration file is YAML format. Example:
.sp
.EX
.nf
runtime:
  user: appuser
  group: appgroup
  env:
    LOG_LEVEL: info
  signal_forward: true

security:
  no_new_privs: true
  writable_paths:
    - /tmp

secrets:
  file_to_env:
    - file: /run/secrets/db_password
      env_var: DB_PASSWORD

lifecycle:
  pre_start:
    command: /app/migrate.sh
    timeout_secs: 30

app:
  readiness:
    http_get:
      path: /health
      port: 8080
.EE
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B UENTRY_STRICT
Enable strict mode (\fItrue\fR/\fIfalse\fR)
.TP
.B UENTRY_USER
User to run as (username or UID)
.TP
.B UENTRY_GROUP
Group to run as (groupname or GID)
.TP
.B UENTRY_CWD
Working directory
.TP
.B UENTRY_PROFILE
Configuration profile name
.TP
.B UENTRY_CONFIG
Path to configuration file
.TP
.B UENTRY_LOG_FORMAT
Log format (\fItext\fR or \fIjson\fR)
.TP
.B UENTRY_LOG_LEVEL
Log level (\fItrace\fR, \fIdebug\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIwarn\fR, \fIerror\fR)
.TP
.B UENTRY_AUDIT
Enable audit reporting (\fItrue\fR/\fIfalse\fR)
.TP
.B UENTRY_AUDIT_DEEP
Enable deep audit tracing (\fItrue\fR/\fIfalse\fR)
.TP
.B UENTRY_AUDIT_OUTPUT
Audit report output path
.TP
.B UENTRY_AUDIT_PROFILE_OUTPUT
Discovered profile snippet output path
.TP
.B UENTRY_AUDIT_BACKEND
Audit backend (\fIauto\fR, \fIstrace\fR, \fInone\fR)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic usage:
.EX
uentry -- nginx -g "daemon off;"
.EE
.TP
With profile:
.EX
uentry --profile web -- /app/server
.EE
.TP
Strict mode with privilege dropping:
.EX
UENTRY_USER=1000 UENTRY_GROUP=1000 uentry --strict -- /app/app
.EE
.TP
Audit profile discovery:
.EX
uentry --audit --audit-output /tmp/audit.json --audit-profile-output /tmp/profile.yaml -- /app/app
.EE
.TP
With configuration file:
.EX
uentry --config /etc/uentry/config.yaml -- /app/app
.EE
.TP
Run diagnostics:
.EX
uentry --diagnose
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/uentry/config.yaml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/uentry/profiles/*.yaml
Custom profile definitions.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/uentry/hooks/{phase}.d/*
External lifecycle hooks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (child exited with code 0)
.TP
.B 1-125
Child process exit code
.TP
.B 126
Command not executable
.TP
.B 127
Command not found
.TP
.B 128+n
Child killed by signal n
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR podman (1),
.BR tini (1)
